# FFXII 1.0.4.0 function overrides and discovered continuation sites.
#
# The lifter reads catch funclets, unwind actions, catch continuations and
# __except targets from the image itself, so they need no lines here.
# Diagnostic probes (probe <VA> <name>) go here while a diagnosis runs and
# come out afterwards: a probe site is an entry and splits its function.

entry 00861ED8 VCRUNTIME140.DLL::__C_specific_handler

# Import thunk of __intrinsic_setjmp. Its callers are luaD_rawrunprotected
# (0081E050, Lua 5.2.1) and three functions near 0016E4A0. longjmp is an
# import the runtime handles, so it needs no resume site.
setjmp 00861EF6 VCRUNTIME140.DLL::__intrinsic_setjmp

# Switch tables Ghidra exported wrong: target = image base + dword[table + 4i],
# read from the image with the bound from the cmp/ja before each dispatch
# (2026-11-20). 007137BA was missing case 0 and the default: after New Game
# the boot hit "branch at 007137BA to 007137BC outside lifted code".
jumptable 0037C4C9 0037C4CB,0037C4E0,0037C550,0037C566,0037C59B,0037C5AD,0037C62A,0037C656,0037C661,0037C689,0037C6C3
jumptable 0058064F 00580651,00580750,005806A4,005806CC,005806E5,00580711,0058072D,0058074B
jumptable 007137BA 007137BC,007137BF,00713782,007137C5,007137CB,007137D1,007137D7
# Two-level table (byte index at 0071B710, 36 cases) in a function Ghidra missed.
entry 0071B6B0
jumptable 0071B6D8 0071B6DA,0071B6E2,0071B6EA,0071B6F2,0071B6F7

# Indirect tail calls (jmp through a function-pointer register) that
# jumptables.tsv lists as switches with only the targets Ghidra saw. After
# New Game the boot hit "branch at 00254937 to 002E1CA0 outside lifted code".
tailcall 00237074
tailcall 00254836
tailcall 00254937
tailcall 002549E2
tailcall 003050FE
tailcall 0039021C
tailcall 0039027C
tailcall 0050556C
tailcall 007FA648
tailcall 00809958
tailcall 0085E686
tailcall 0085E6F9
tailcall 00883342

# 2026-11-20 static audit of every indirect jmp in .text (981 reached sites,
# scripts in the session scratchpad audit/audit.py). Classes: 503 switch
# tables whose targets I recomputed from the table and cmp/ja bound (all
# match jumptables.tsv except the four fixed above); 245 jmp [rip+x] import
# thunks or pointer hooks, 177 jmp [reg+off] / [table+reg*8] vtable and
# pointer-table tail calls, 48 jmp reg tail calls through a loaded pointer
# (none of these need a row). One more tail call still had a Ghidra row:
# a counter hook that jumps through a function pointer.
tailcall 0085E71B

# Loose-file mod override (src/mods.cpp, analysis/formats/
# vbf-runtime-read-path.md): VBF Find, Reader::Read and reader release.
replace 0019AEE0
replace 00215110
replace 002150D0

# Field-interaction probe (src/probe.cpp, FFXII_PROBE=1): talk flags,
# talk target, ellipse distance, facing test.
replace 002E0FA0
replace 002647D0
replace 003DA5A0
replace 003A1BB0

# Import stubs of VCRUNTIME140 memcpy and memset (tools/find_crt_stubs.py,
# 2026-11-22). Direct calls to them are done inline: the render thread's copy
# loops (f_00628B40) spent most of their time spilling registers around them.
crt 00861EBA memcpy
crt 00861EC0 memset

# Frame-timing globals (src/frame_rate.cpp, FFXII_SIM_MULT=k experiment).
replace 001EDDC0
replace 006234A0
replace 00248030
replace 00259240
replace 00250540
replace 00250730
replace 0022B6E0
replace 0022B8C0
replace 002507C0
replace 003820C0
replace 0022A770
replace 0060EC80
